      "text": [
        " أَدْنَى مَا تَحِلُّ بِهِ الْمُتْعَةُ كَفٌّ مِنْ طَعَامٍ وَ رَوَى بَعْضُهُمْ مِسْوَاكٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Muhammad Bin Isa, from Yunus, from one of our companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The lowest of what the <span class=\"iTxt\">Mut’a</span> is Permissible with, is a handful of foodstuff’. And some of them have reported, ‘One toothbrush (twig)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Yunus from certain persons of our people who have said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The minimum amount of mahr (dower) in al-Mut‘ah (advantageous marriage) can be even a handful of food.’ Certain ones of them have narrated that even a Miswak (toothbrush) is acceptable.” "
        ]
      }
    },
